  <page_number>95</page_number>
  <running_head>LYRICA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <p><i>Prolem lacteolo lætior vbere:</i></p>
    <p><i>In partémque iuuat domum</i></p>
    <p><i>Et quacunque labor coniugis inuehit</i></p>
    <p><i>Dispensat bene prouida.</i></p>
    <p><i>Ast inuisa Deo gens pereat malè,</i></p>
    <p><i>Audax nubere quæ vetat:</i></p>
    <p><i>Quæ vanis simulans religionibus</i></p>
    <p><i>Cultus impia Cœlitum</i></p>
    <p><i>Damnat legitimas connubij faces.</i></p>
    <p><i>Vita cœlibe quæ putat</i></p>
    <p><i>Se diuûm meritis sedibus inseri.</i></p>
    <p><i>Nonne his putida fontibus</i></p>
    <p><i>Erumpens scelerum colluuies tetris,</i></p>
    <p><i>Incestare domos solet?</i></p>
    <p><i>Nonne hæc vota semel virginitas stupris</i></p>
    <p><i>Vicos polluit urbium,</i></p>
    <p><i>Et Claustra horrificis cædibus inquinat?</i></p>
    <p><i>Sed quæ legibus obsequi</i></p>
    <p><i>Gens puris didicit, dogmata Dæmonis,</i></p>
    <p><i>Fucatósque procul dolos</i></p>
    <p><i>Depellit Stygÿ: nec reputat nefas</i></p>
    <p><i>Lucis conscia Olympicæ</i></p>
    <p><i>Concessis Superûm muneribus frui.</i></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printed ornament (fleuron) below the verse is not transcribed as text. Some letters in the verse are doubtful due to scan quality, notably "Nonne his putida" and "Erumpens scelerum colluuies".</notes>
